===Etymology===
;lift
:May be cognate with {{cog|bo|འཁྱོག་པ||to lift; to bring; to carry}}, {{cog|bo|སྐྱ་བ||to carry; to convey}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}). Alternatively, it may be related to {{och-l|舁|to lift}} as a ''*k-'' prefixed verb ({{zh-ref|Baxter and Sagart, 1998}}).

;all, whole, entire
:{{der|zh|sit}}. Cognate with {{cog|tbq-lob-pro|*ka||all}} (STEDT, {{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}})
;to pawn
:The [[counter]] of the [[pawnbroker]] is usually at a high position. Therefore, customers must lift the object to be pawned at a pawn shop.

