;"to stop, to halt, to rest" > "resting place" > "lodging house"
:Apparently shared with {{cog|qfa-kms-pro|tr=*s-lwa<sup>B</sup>}}; Proto-Chinese root must have been *''s-lwas'', identical to PKS, with OC *''sl-'' > *''lh-'' and MC {{zh-l|去聲}} (from *''-h'' < *''-s'') corresponding to KS tone B ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}). Schuessler further relates {{och-l|舍|tr=*lhah}} to {{zh-l|説|tr=shuì|to halt, to rest overnight}} < OC *''lho(t)s'' < *''lhuats'', which, being a closed syllable, reflexes Proto-Chinese medial *''-w-''; unlike {{zh-l|舍}} < MC *''ɕia<sup>H</sup>'' < OC *''lhah'', an open syllable whose phonological structure (at least in MC) did not allow medial *''-w-''. Schuessler concludes: "The ambivalence in the forms, as in the finals in these two words, is typical for loan words".

