===Glyph origin===
{{Han etym}}
{{Han compound|艸|alt1=艹|化|ls=psc|c1=s|c2=p|t1=grass; plant}}. Originally {{zh-l|*𠌶}} or {{zh-l|*華}} before the {{w|Han dynasty}}.

===Etymology===
Unclear. 

Possibly of {{der|zh|sit}} origin. {{zh-ref|Schuessler (2007)}} derives it from {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*baːr||bloom, flower}} and thus an example of possible *''b'' ~ *''w'' variation, with final ''-r'' moved to medial position. If so, cognate with {{ltc-l|葩}}; outside {{w|Sinitic languages|Sinitic}}, compare {{cog|my|ပန်း}}, {{cog|lep|ᰓᰫᰲ|tr=búr}}, {{cog|lus|páar}}, etc. {{zh-ref|Sagart (2021)}} also connects it to {{och-l|葩|tr=*pʰˤra}}, modifying {{zh-ref|Baxter and Sagart's (2014)}} reconstruction to ''*Cə-pʰˤra'' and proposing the sound changes *''Cə-pʰ-'' > *''Cə-ɸ-'' > *''ɸ-'' > ''xw-''.

{{zh-ref|Sagart & Baxter (2024)}} reconstruct {{och-l|荂|tr= *pʰra}} ~ {{och-l|葩|tr= *pʰˤra}} and {{och-l|荂|tr= *X.pʰra}} ~ {{och-l|花|tr= *X.pʰˤra}} (with unknown prefix {{IPAfont|*X}} turning labial stops into {{w|Middle Chinese}} fricative initials in  {{ltc-l|荂|id=1}} ~ {{ltc-l|花}}) (which might have already happened by the time of the {{w|Western Zhou}} dynasty, as shown by the presence of the {{och-l|于}} radical in its earliest form {{ltc-l|𦻏}}). Furthermore, they propose cognacy to {{cog|kar-pro|*phɔᴬ||flower}} and reconstruct {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*p(h)a||[[idem]]}}. Outside Sino-Tibetan, they propose cognacy to {{cog|map-pro|*pahpah||flower, petal; leaf}}.

Alternatively, from {{der|zh|aav}}; compare {{cog|aav-pro|*bka(ː)ʔ||flower}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).

{{och-l|華|id=2|to flower}} is a derivative.

